 "Open race with a term-limited Republican president, so the GOP gets no incumbent advantage", "Recent presidential results in the state have run well ahead of its partisan lean", "The 2026 primary upset of the state's Democratic governor signals local voter frustration and adds uncertainty"], "rationale": "Rhode Island's eight-point Democratic lean and its history of double-digit presidential margins point to a clear Democratic edge, and the term-limited Republican incumbent leaves the president's party without an incumbent advantage. With no polls, ratings, or market data available, uncertainty stays high and the race remains in Lean D.", "watch": "The first credible general-election polls or expert ratings, or a shift in the national mood after two terms of Republican control, could move this forecast several points in either direction.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island enters the 2028 presidential race without an incumbent on the ballot, as the sitting Republican president is term-limited. The state's partisan lean favors Democrats by eight points, and its recent presidential voting has generally run even more Democratic than that lean implies. No public polls, expert ratings, or market prices exist for this contest, so the outlook rests on fundamentals alone.\n\nUncertainty is wide. Local Democratic cohesion is not automatic: the state's Democratic governor lost a 2026 primary amid anger over a bridge project, a sign of voter frustration that could spill into other races. Still, a Republican win here would likely require a substantial national shift, since Rhode Island has been reliably Democratic at the presidential level. The race currently rates as a Democratic lean, with wide error bands until real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8249, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7734, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7988, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7688, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8114, "margin": 9.0}]}